1- client-server archetecture

this architecture is the foundation of APIs
it dictates how 2 independent systems find, talk and exchange data with each other!

API exists between the client and the server, it mediates and facilates the communication!

a- the client:
the client is any application or user-interfaces and data or computation performed
it starts the conversation by sending an HTTP request

examples:
    react single page on the web
    IOS mobile app
    CLI script

--> these examples right here, dont know how the program works under the hood, it only knows the API rule to send requests


b- the server:
the server is the backend infrastructure, such as fastapi

examples:
    python/fastapi app
    node.js api
    database server

--> these examples listen to incoming requests, validates them, perform the task and returns the requested data


