2- REST API:
REST is an architecture style that operates strictly on the traditional HTTP request-response cycle
with JSON as the standard language for data exchange

to qualify as REST API, it must adher to these constrains:
statelessness: 
    every request from the client must be self-contained 
    this means it must contain all the info the server needs to send back requested data
    api doesnt remember previous requests, every request must be self-contained

standard HTTP methods (verbs):
    GET:            retrieve data
    POST:           create new data
    PUT / PATCH:    updata data
    DELETE:         remove data


